#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198227 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a5637d71-22d4-548e-ad36-d09bff61d643" :question/math-academy-id "e-2398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198230 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c737d317-8e09-5ccb-b816-b5f56e925ba9" :question/math-academy-id "e-609" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198231 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "cde8f304-4937-5eb7-a8e1-a08355ee4d4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-611" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db3f942-5a8e-5c2a-9795-e961f39580cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300006} {:answer/id #uuid "59f11bd6-b9db-576a-845f-5008a1c945f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300430} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1ab615-f3d9-5c6e-be11-88b45849bbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-5{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300431} {:answer/id #uuid "8710fa72-9009-525d-ae96-e335042f6b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j+\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300641} {:answer/id #uuid "b90224c9-aa56-5a7b-91b0-1356c9aead70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{1-{t}^{2}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59f11bd6-b9db-576a-845f-5008a1c945f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300430} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eb0988d-ace0-5f09-b160-12ad3b3114c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d5868b7-9316-570b-b593-afbcd34e82e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-32417" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡3t\\,i-5{t}^{4}\\,j+\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$  by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡3t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}})\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "594d297d-4ffa-5fcd-8767-7af6f4ed264d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500650} {:answer/id #uuid "7e43eea9-78bb-565d-8191-43c478367b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500729} {:answer/id #uuid "82e99160-4a68-56e8-a3ef-7b8309c26551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j-\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500738} {:answer/id #uuid "c255f2ae-f1e7-5320-99a1-222b7be0cc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500872} {:answer/id #uuid "c78884eb-c06b-51c6-b4c7-0f6e4cc6678d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c78884eb-c06b-51c6-b4c7-0f6e4cc6678d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500890} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f0a5f53-2383-5407-951d-8f444396db3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66e3887f-e0ed-593b-b271-ae704cd5f2f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-34720" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b9fceca-75ad-51bc-ae92-c08f9fc2becc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500524} {:answer/id #uuid "21637f5f-66fc-5d10-9eec-a98e25102b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500537} {:answer/id #uuid "5e8fe481-3298-52af-9b2d-8bc1094ba831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500662} {:answer/id #uuid "85151a70-250f-5968-b519-91999091ac9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500743} {:answer/id #uuid "c51b200a-ecff-5cd9-93e9-8afa94661d25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡4s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85151a70-250f-5968-b519-91999091ac9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500743} :answer-field/id #uuid "4afb8b57-1fee-58f6-a694-2fa66ad992b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f415e47a-854d-5840-b197-b8e66cc67e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-34722" :question/problem "Calculate the second derivative of  $f(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩$ with respect to $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(s)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(s)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d8f4b31-7cd4-567a-b1ab-e1908f4c5bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-2{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391892} {:answer/id #uuid "770c4032-8926-5b49-96b8-17c721eb3eeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }\\,i-{e}^{\\pi }\\,j+{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391893} {:answer/id #uuid "d767d08e-9f3d-5075-804a-e32b3b238995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391894} {:answer/id #uuid "53ba9a50-f890-5647-8a42-ad787ec3b6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391895} {:answer/id #uuid "fadb0885-54d3-518c-85c6-6d456aea62cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53ba9a50-f890-5647-8a42-ad787ec3b6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391895} :answer-field/id #uuid "1620165b-3bcb-5548-8049-48ba8d5cc382" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e579ce0-d5f9-57b8-931d-2fc18fc335d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-34724" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)={e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ at $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =({e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +{e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j+({e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -{e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{\\pi }\\cdot 0+{e}^{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j+({e}^{\\pi }\\cdot (-1)-{e}^{\\pi }\\cdot 0)\\,k \\\\  & =-{e}^{\\pi }\\,i+{e}^{\\pi }\\,j-{e}^{\\pi }\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e24d1ecc-57dc-5c33-9cba-5e409dfc2302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.typ