 :answer/value "2\\ln(3)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eec3fb3-98bb-539f-828a-96203367f774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln(3)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500764} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bfa90a3-ba24-559f-9c8b-5a07e671e7fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11cf7146-ed56-5694-a708-a9b3016a6fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11cf7146-ed56-5694-a708-a9b3016a6fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500506} :answer-field/id #uuid "504d5d52-6b4f-57e5-9c75-2dca13703f87" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc780555-5bb0-55aa-b97f-a47fa4610bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc780555-5bb0-55aa-b97f-a47fa4610bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500860} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4dc9af4-ea47-5fb1-8da7-ddafaed28423" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87416abb-dad9-5afe-bb9d-e8fcd5a9095c" :question/math-academy-id "q-350227" :question/problem "Given that  $f(t)=2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)\\,i-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\frac{6}{t}\\,k,$   what is ${f}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${f}^{′}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j\\,\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$k$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t))\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{6}{t})\\,k \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)+2)\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot 1)+2)\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\,j-\\frac{6}{{1}^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡1\\,j-6\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61d7cc13-045d-5dfc-8f21-557e9035974d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60t^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61d7cc13-045d-5dfc-8f21-557e9035974d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60t^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500669} :answer-field/id #uuid "9181ccb7-fad9-5675-90e4-730835fd6807" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51e9395c-263f-51bd-b6a4-d472df228bdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{t^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e9395c-263f-51bd-b6a4-d472df228bdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{t^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500636} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2548aa-0d72-568a-936f-6eb2f6da4f5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3300ef54-fdde-5f40-809c-0c4bab2d0166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{1-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3300ef54-fdde-5f40-809c-0c4bab2d0166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{1-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500576} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0de4306-091e-529b-ae8c-530f65ea903f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cc15b80-72fe-59a5-9238-583abab2565e" :question/math-academy-id "q-350802" :question/problem "Determine ${f}^{″}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{t} \\\\ {e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -2{t}^{6}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{″}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{1-2t})\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{6})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ -2{e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -12{t}^{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{e}^{1-2t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-12{t}^{5})\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3/2}} \\\\ 4{e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -60{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fde686e-0040-50c8-9b9b-1ad4f1e8aaa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392724} {:answer/id #uuid "d02ac812-19ad-5839-9ad9-16c2a59beade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392725} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4ffd3e-cd2a-5031-83aa-72de86237fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392726} {:answer/id #uuid "dd140ea3-6577-5157-ab09-4fefef73b8e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392727} {:answer/id #uuid "37a5973e-637b-5d29-9329-f2c326b69242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d02ac812-19ad-5839-9ad9-16c2a59beade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392725} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ef94ed-b793-5302-a468-c42ecf1df591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "607151f7-a0f9-522f-b6fe-540456f7af54" :question/math-academy-id "q-50371" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60877467-26a5-565e-9a60-7a1ac5cca6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330808} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9e1b5e-3926-5b9a-ae3b-e6b881cd6740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330907} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc6346e-b150-5374-a32d-4d1a5ec7bc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330933} {:answer/id #uuid "86448057-4fd0-59f3-ba66-fd86d9b805be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331142} {:answer/id #uuid "d2236804-95e9-51ec-8331-608fbaf4e7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9e1b5e-3926-5b9a-ae3b-e6b881cd6740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330907} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af1f59d-cae6-5771-b8c0-f4f36400d291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf813be6-995c-5d07-9a48-ae4dc989093b" :question/math-academy-id "q-50373" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06006b25-a443-54f2-8024-d157cc2b8a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500478} {:answer/id #uuid "4eee71c6-18a3-564f-aef0-94f6b2a849b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500627} {:answer/id #uuid "67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500681} {:answer/id #uuid "da6cdfe0-793c-5d04-b91f-02dd3f4e71ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500932} {:answer/id #uuid "ff20f98e-9f1b-5ada-b97d-a2fe856607b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d97608c5-ec21-5589-b8cb-89d769aeba4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bf645e6-f706-50ea-8450-5ddbc0499160" :question/math-academy-id "q-50377" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4t-10,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe19103f-5f99-576d-a025-053904208525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392731} {:answer/id #uuid "e01882fe-f747-5560-b961-3aeaa74d08c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{3}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392732} {:answer/id #uuid "574da43a-a87f-5e11-8117-2e74261fac00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392733} {:answer/id #uuid "8eccfb9d-3d94-5276-98aa-105bb31f0184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392734} {:answer/id #uuid "13350f1d-caa5-59e1-8249-6fc0fdc305b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "574da43a-a87f-5e11-8117-2e74261fac00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392733} :answer-field/id #uuid "30603a02-99ff-59c6-861c-ce870828f5cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7fd0a18c-43f2-5761-ad4b-96e6a87257fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-50467" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1655080f-c794-53f9-9762-71446a1428b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24{t}^{3},\\,16{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500517} {:answer/id #uuid "4aa25a3e-ad0c-5469-b35f-f6b463e1bf29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12t,\\,-12{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500617} {:answer/id #uuid "4de7e70a-49ca-5324-89ae-72cc0b88d9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24{t}^{2},\\,36t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500626} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec79135-6f74-58f5-be5f-857da38fc279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500693} {:answer/id #uuid "ce607db8-3e5f-5aee-be46-05f404a110b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-36t,\\,24{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ec79135-6f74-58f5-be5f-857da38fc279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500693} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad618895-a9b2-5479-91a2-b7889155fabf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b01d0b7-5c1a-5382-b422-a24594a7e8ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-75033" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4{t}^{3}-t,\\,7t-3{t}^{4}⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=4{t}^{3}-t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =12{t}^{2}-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=7t-3{t}^{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =7-12{t}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-36{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d7d4f9-cc8a-581c-be35-d8f2ce13846a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342837} {:answer/id #uuid "85e5795d-b19e-5643-a38f-a0da7b3d6d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343388} {:answer/id #uuid "bbafed32-dd0f-5c01-9a8e-7410fedcd53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343887} {:answer/id #uuid "c9fc8dac-5428-55ea-966a-6e8f824e3ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+2\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344012} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaf2a04-fd6e-55b0-8db0-5b009d339897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85e5795d-b19e-5643-a38f-a0da7b3d6d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343388} :answer-field/id #uuid "232e97df-a9bc-5885-b743-1f8a9e12529e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a91bca78-5c50-5527-ac8e-ebf8cd03d30a" :question/math-academy-id "q-77678" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-5t)\\,j+\\frac{1}{1+t}\\,k$ at $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-5t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{1+t})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,i+(6t-5)\\,j-\\frac{1}{(1+t)^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1)$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{1+(1)^{2}}\\,i+(6(1)-5)\\,j-\\frac{1}{(1+(1))^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
